{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"issue-1898-relation-filter-review","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Issue #1898 relation-filter review"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"scope-and-evidence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scope and evidence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Base: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afbeb44eef48d92b6e30ae5fd2843b938ee9163c"},{"type":"text","value":". The issue and its\nSeptember 25 author comment contain 26 distinct claims, proposals, and open\nquestions. The executable owner is\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/tests/query/ordered-work-oracle.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"; the ordered\nlifecycle and pagination oracles are adjacent owners. This review covers one\ndirect LEFT join to a Collection with direct root ordering. It does not prove\nremote relation filtering or a changed-FK failure. Finite continuation also\nrequires an order index; without one, the existing full-source fallback can\nstill apply after an underfilled prefix."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recent merged work covered adjacent paths: #1893 fixed indexed multi-term\npaging, #1903 replaced fragmented lazy join demand after churn, and #1904\ndefined the custom-collation full-source boundary. None removed the\ncross-alias full-source branch exercised here."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before this change, the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"some"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"none"},{"type":"text","value":", joined-only, and to-one work cells\nall requested a full root source. The anti-join Effect cell also emitted a\nmatched root that was absent from the independent result. After the change,\nthe focused owner passes all 86 tests. A controlled mutant that removes the\njoined-demand gate starts three root pages before the child settles where the\noracle permits one; it also publishes an incorrect anti-join window. Restoring\nthe gate makes those cells pass. A 42-root fixture stops after fewer than ten\nrequests when the first roots satisfy the joined filter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lossless-issue-ledger","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lossless issue ledger"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The IDs follow the issue body ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"I"},{"type":"text","value":") and author comment ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"C"},{"type":"text","value":") in source order.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fixed-now"},{"type":"text","value":" refers to the accompanying implementation. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deferred"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"design-decision"},{"type":"text","value":" remain tracked by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/issues/1898","children":[{"type":"text","value":"issue #1898"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ID"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disposition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evidence, limit, or next step"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I01"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed-now"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The original direct LEFT-join query requested an unbounded root snapshot. The oracle now requires a finite first page and checks the independent result."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I02"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed-now"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A controlled unresolved child request plus a disabled-gate mutant proves root pagination can outrun child demand."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I03"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specify "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LoadSubsetOptions.relations"},{"type":"text","value":", including the superset rule for adapters that ignore a hint. No hint is emitted in this change."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I04"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"design-decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"every(p) = none(not p)"},{"type":"text","value":" holds for a two-valued predicate and an empty relation. Define nullable expression semantics before making it an adapter law."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I05"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The compiler now permits local finite paging for one direct LEFT join. It does not extract AND conjuncts into remote relation hints or cover joined subqueries."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I06"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once hints exist, propagate the same hint through initial, refill, repair, and tie requests; test request identity and acquisition release."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I07"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed-now"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Root continuation waits for unsettled lazy demand or a joined subscription load. Settlement and status changes rerun the loader."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I08"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed-now"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A joined-side delete now reruns ordered loading and refills both Collection and Effect windows."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I09"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Include future relation hints in exact demand identity so narrowed and unrestricted acquisitions cannot cover one another."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The reported honored-hint request and row counts are fixture measurements. Test a real hint-aware adapter after the API exists."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I11"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed-now"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without a relation hint, local evaluation reaches exact pages from a finite prefix; a 42-root fixture stops early. The author's precise prototype counts are not universal laws."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I12"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"already-fixed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eager local Collections already returned the correct result; the oracle retains that control."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I13"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This change proves a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"some"},{"type":"text","value":" child deletion refills the window. Add insert/delete histories for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"some"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"none"},{"type":"text","value":", and nullable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"every"},{"type":"text","value":" semantics."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I14"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed-now"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The controlled gate mutant overfetches before child settlement. The reported 40 ms and 40-row values are timing-specific observations."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I15"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"design-decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decide whether a future relation hint applies to unlimited queries; this implementation only changes finite windows."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I16"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"design-decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The query-wide gate can delay an unrelated include. Measure dependency-specific latency before adding per-join state."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I17"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Joined subqueries and unsupported plans retain full-source fallback. Direct-join "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OR"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NOT"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the same local prefix law but needs dedicated oracle cells; remote hint extraction must stay conservative."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I18"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify cursor and offset coverage when another query has installed root rows and when a backend narrows rows by relation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C01"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed-now"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A direct to-one PK equality join has the same full-source branch and now pages finitely. A distinct root-FK fixture remains useful."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C02"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"design-decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"some(conjunct)"},{"type":"text","value":" is exact when the conjunct fails on a missing joined row; require a semantic proof and nullable tests before emitting the hint."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C03"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"design-decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"none(not conjunct)"},{"type":"text","value":" for a conjunct that passes on a missing row requires at most one matching child. Multiple matches give a counterexample."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C04"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"refuted"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sentinel "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getKey({id: sentinel}) === sentinel"},{"type":"text","value":" probe cannot establish uniqueness: a key function can return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenant:id"},{"type":"text","value":" for real rows while passing that probe. Use an explicit uniqueness contract."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C05"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The comment reports honored/ignored hints, skip, eager, and live coverage. This change covers local paging, eager control, and some live updates; the full hint matrix remains."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C06"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"InstantDB's 30 s and 1.5 s measurements are external observations; no in-repository backend trace verifies them."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C07"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"design-decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A filtered prefix of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offset + limit"},{"type":"text","value":" can cover a cursor window if offset bounds the count of passing rows before the cursor. Prove that premise for each adapter and document the strategy."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C08"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"confirmed-open"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A current-main probe with both children installed and child "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadSubset"},{"type":"text","value":" returning without writes updated correctly after a root FK change. The exact failing precondition is unknown; a clarification request is posted on the issue."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Totals: 7 fixed-now, 1 already-fixed, 10 deferred, 6 design-decision,\n1 refuted, and 1 confirmed-open; 26 source items accounted for."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"remaining-design-work","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remaining design work"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The largest next step is a safe relation hint. It needs a syntax classifier, a\nproof that hints only narrow to a superset of the local result, request plumbing\nthrough tie and repair paths, and exact demand identity. The sentinel key probe\nfrom the comment must not certify to-one joins. A second investigation should\nreproduce the changed-FK case under the author's adapter behavior before\naltering the lazy-join lifecycle."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"issue-1898-relation-filter-review","text":"Issue #1898 relation-filter review","level":1},{"id":"scope-and-evidence","text":"Scope and evidence","level":2},{"id":"lossless-issue-ledger","text":"Lossless issue ledger","level":2},{"id":"remaining-design-work","text":"Remaining design work","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Issue #1898 relation-filter review\n\n## Scope and evidence\n\nBase: `afbeb44eef48d92b6e30ae5fd2843b938ee9163c`. The issue and its\nSeptember 25 author comment contain 26 distinct claims, proposals, and open\nquestions. The executable owner is\n`packages/db/tests/query/ordered-work-oracle.property.test.ts`; the ordered\nlifecycle and pagination oracles are adjacent owners. This review covers one\ndirect LEFT join to a Collection with direct root ordering. It does not prove\nremote relation filtering or a changed-FK failure. Finite continuation also\nrequires an order index; without one, the existing full-source fallback can\nstill apply after an underfilled prefix.\n\nRecent merged work covered adjacent paths: #1893 fixed indexed multi-term\npaging, #1903 replaced fragmented lazy join demand after churn, and #1904\ndefined the custom-collation full-source boundary. None removed the\ncross-alias full-source branch exercised here.\n\nBefore this change, the new `some`, `none`, joined-only, and to-one work cells\nall requested a full root source. The anti-join Effect cell also emitted a\nmatched root that was absent from the independent result. After the change,\nthe focused owner passes all 86 tests. A controlled mutant that removes the\njoined-demand gate starts three root pages before the child settles where the\noracle permits one; it also publishes an incorrect anti-join window. Restoring\nthe gate makes those cells pass. A 42-root fixture stops after fewer than ten\nrequests when the first roots satisfy the joined filter.\n\n## Lossless issue ledger\n\nThe IDs follow the issue body (`I`) and author comment (`C`) in source order.\n`fixed-now` refers to the accompanying implementation. `deferred` and\n`design-decision` remain tracked by [issue #1898](https://github.com/TanStack/db/issues/1898).\n\n| ID | Disposition | Evidence, limit, or next step |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| I01 | fixed-now | The original direct LEFT-join query requested an unbounded root snapshot. The oracle now requires a finite first page and checks the independent result. |\n| I02 | fixed-now | A controlled unresolved child request plus a disabled-gate mutant proves root pagination can outrun child demand. |\n| I03 | deferred | Specify `LoadSubsetOptions.relations`, including the superset rule for adapters that ignore a hint. No hint is emitted in this change. |\n| I04 | design-decision | `every(p) = none(not p)` holds for a two-valued predicate and an empty relation. Define nullable expression semantics before making it an adapter law. |\n| I05 | deferred | The compiler now permits local finite paging for one direct LEFT join. It does not extract AND conjuncts into remote relation hints or cover joined subqueries. |\n| I06 | deferred | Once hints exist, propagate the same hint through initial, refill, repair, and tie requests; test request identity and acquisition release. |\n| I07 | fixed-now | Root continuation waits for unsettled lazy demand or a joined subscription load. Settlement and status changes rerun the loader. |\n| I08 | fixed-now | A joined-side delete now reruns ordered loading and refills both Collection and Effect windows. |\n| I09 | deferred | Include future relation hints in exact demand identity so narrowed and unrestricted acquisitions cannot cover one another. |\n| I10 | deferred | The reported honored-hint request and row counts are fixture measurements. Test a real hint-aware adapter after the API exists. |\n| I11 | fixed-now | Without a relation hint, local evaluation reaches exact pages from a finite prefix; a 42-root fixture stops early. The author's precise prototype counts are not universal laws. |\n| I12 | already-fixed | Eager local Collections already returned the correct result; the oracle retains that control. |\n| I13 | deferred | This change proves a `some` child deletion refills the window. Add insert/delete histories for `some`, `none`, and nullable `every` semantics. |\n| I14 | fixed-now | The controlled gate mutant overfetches before child settlement. The reported 40 ms and 40-row values are timing-specific observations. |\n| I15 | design-decision | Decide whether a future relation hint applies to unlimited queries; this implementation only changes finite windows. |\n| I16 | design-decision | The query-wide gate can delay an unrelated include. Measure dependency-specific latency before adding per-join state. |\n| I17 | deferred | Joined subqueries and unsupported plans retain full-source fallback. Direct-join `OR`/`NOT` uses the same local prefix law but needs dedicated oracle cells; remote hint extraction must stay conservative. |\n| I18 | deferred | Verify cursor and offset coverage when another query has installed root rows and when a backend narrows rows by relation. |\n| C01 | fixed-now | A direct to-one PK equality join has the same full-source branch and now pages finitely. A distinct root-FK fixture remains useful. |\n| C02 | design-decision | `some(conjunct)` is exact when the conjunct fails on a missing joined row; require a semantic proof and nullable tests before emitting the hint. |\n| C03 | design-decision | `none(not conjunct)` for a conjunct that passes on a missing row requires at most one matching child. Multiple matches give a counterexample. |\n| C04 | refuted | A sentinel `getKey({id: sentinel}) === sentinel` probe cannot establish uniqueness: a key function can return `tenant:id` for real rows while passing that probe. Use an explicit uniqueness contract. |\n| C05 | deferred | The comment reports honored/ignored hints, skip, eager, and live coverage. This change covers local paging, eager control, and some live updates; the full hint matrix remains. |\n| C06 | deferred | InstantDB's 30 s and 1.5 s measurements are external observations; no in-repository backend trace verifies them. |\n| C07 | design-decision | A filtered prefix of `offset + limit` can cover a cursor window if offset bounds the count of passing rows before the cursor. Prove that premise for each adapter and document the strategy. |\n| C08 | confirmed-open | A current-main probe with both children installed and child `loadSubset` returning without writes updated correctly after a root FK change. The exact failing precondition is unknown; a clarification request is posted on the issue. |\n\nTotals: 7 fixed-now, 1 already-fixed, 10 deferred, 6 design-decision,\n1 refuted, and 1 confirmed-open; 26 source items accounted for.\n\n## Remaining design work\n\nThe largest next step is a safe relation hint. It needs a syntax classifier, a\nproof that hints only narrow to a superset of the local result, request plumbing\nthrough tie and repair paths, and exact demand identity. The sentinel key probe\nfrom the comment must not certify to-one joins. A second investigation should\nreproduce the changed-FK case under the author's adapter behavior before\naltering the lazy-join lifecycle.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Issue #1898 relation-filter review\n\n## Scope and evidence\n\nBase: `afbeb44eef48d92b6e30ae5fd2843b938ee9163c`. The issue and its\nSeptember 25 author comment contain 26 distinct claims, proposals, and open\nquestions. The executable owner is\n`packages/db/tests/query/ordered-work-oracle.property.test.ts`; the ordered\nlifecycle and pagination oracles are adjacent owners. This review covers one\ndirect LEFT join to a Collection with direct root ordering. It does not prove\nremote relation filtering or a changed-FK failure. Finite continuation also\nrequires an order index; without one, the existing full-source fallback can\nstill apply after an underfilled prefix.\n\nRecent merged work covered adjacent paths: #1893 fixed indexed multi-term\npaging, #1903 replaced fragmented lazy join demand after churn, and #1904\ndefined the custom-collation full-source boundary. None removed the\ncross-alias full-source branch exercised here.\n\nBefore this change, the new `some`, `none`, joined-only, and to-one work cells\nall requested a full root source. The anti-join Effect cell also emitted a\nmatched root that was absent from the independent result. After the change,\nthe focused owner passes all 86 tests. A controlled mutant that removes the\njoined-demand gate starts three root pages before the child settles where the\noracle permits one; it also publishes an incorrect anti-join window. Restoring\nthe gate makes those cells pass. A 42-root fixture stops after fewer than ten\nrequests when the first roots satisfy the joined filter.\n\n## Lossless issue ledger\n\nThe IDs follow the issue body (`I`) and author comment (`C`) in source order.\n`fixed-now` refers to the accompanying implementation. `deferred` and\n`design-decision` remain tracked by [issue #1898](https://github.com/TanStack/db/issues/1898).\n\n| ID | Disposition | Evidence, limit, or next step |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| I01 | fixed-now | The original direct LEFT-join query requested an unbounded root snapshot. The oracle now requires a finite first page and checks the independent result. |\n| I02 | fixed-now | A controlled unresolved child request plus a disabled-gate mutant proves root pagination can outrun child demand. |\n| I03 | deferred | Specify `LoadSubsetOptions.relations`, including the superset rule for adapters that ignore a hint. No hint is emitted in this change. |\n| I04 | design-decision | `every(p) = none(not p)` holds for a two-valued predicate and an empty relation. Define nullable expression semantics before making it an adapter law. |\n| I05 | deferred | The compiler now permits local finite paging for one direct LEFT join. It does not extract AND conjuncts into remote relation hints or cover joined subqueries. |\n| I06 | deferred | Once hints exist, propagate the same hint through initial, refill, repair, and tie requests; test request identity and acquisition release. |\n| I07 | fixed-now | Root continuation waits for unsettled lazy demand or a joined subscription load. Settlement and status changes rerun the loader. |\n| I08 | fixed-now | A joined-side delete now reruns ordered loading and refills both Collection and Effect windows. |\n| I09 | deferred | Include future relation hints in exact demand identity so narrowed and unrestricted acquisitions cannot cover one another. |\n| I10 | deferred | The reported honored-hint request and row counts are fixture measurements. Test a real hint-aware adapter after the API exists. |\n| I11 | fixed-now | Without a relation hint, local evaluation reaches exact pages from a finite prefix; a 42-root fixture stops early. The author's precise prototype counts are not universal laws. |\n| I12 | already-fixed | Eager local Collections already returned the correct result; the oracle retains that control. |\n| I13 | deferred | This change proves a `some` child deletion refills the window. Add insert/delete histories for `some`, `none`, and nullable `every` semantics. |\n| I14 | fixed-now | The controlled gate mutant overfetches before child settlement. The reported 40 ms and 40-row values are timing-specific observations. |\n| I15 | design-decision | Decide whether a future relation hint applies to unlimited queries; this implementation only changes finite windows. |\n| I16 | design-decision | The query-wide gate can delay an unrelated include. Measure dependency-specific latency before adding per-join state. |\n| I17 | deferred | Joined subqueries and unsupported plans retain full-source fallback. Direct-join `OR`/`NOT` uses the same local prefix law but needs dedicated oracle cells; remote hint extraction must stay conservative. |\n| I18 | deferred | Verify cursor and offset coverage when another query has installed root rows and when a backend narrows rows by relation. |\n| C01 | fixed-now | A direct to-one PK equality join has the same full-source branch and now pages finitely. A distinct root-FK fixture remains useful. |\n| C02 | design-decision | `some(conjunct)` is exact when the conjunct fails on a missing joined row; require a semantic proof and nullable tests before emitting the hint. |\n| C03 | design-decision | `none(not conjunct)` for a conjunct that passes on a missing row requires at most one matching child. Multiple matches give a counterexample. |\n| C04 | refuted | A sentinel `getKey({id: sentinel}) === sentinel` probe cannot establish uniqueness: a key function can return `tenant:id` for real rows while passing that probe. Use an explicit uniqueness contract. |\n| C05 | deferred | The comment reports honored/ignored hints, skip, eager, and live coverage. This change covers local paging, eager control, and some live updates; the full hint matrix remains. |\n| C06 | deferred | InstantDB's 30 s and 1.5 s measurements are external observations; no in-repository backend trace verifies them. |\n| C07 | design-decision | A filtered prefix of `offset + limit` can cover a cursor window if offset bounds the count of passing rows before the cursor. Prove that premise for each adapter and document the strategy. |\n| C08 | confirmed-open | A current-main probe with both children installed and child `loadSubset` returning without writes updated correctly after a root FK change. The exact failing precondition is unknown; a clarification request is posted on the issue. |\n\nTotals: 7 fixed-now, 1 already-fixed, 10 deferred, 6 design-decision,\n1 refuted, and 1 confirmed-open; 26 source items accounted for.\n\n## Remaining design work\n\nThe largest next step is a safe relation hint. It needs a syntax classifier, a\nproof that hints only narrow to a superset of the local result, request plumbing\nthrough tie and repair paths, and exact demand identity. The sentinel key probe\nfrom the comment must not certify to-one joins. A second investigation should\nreproduce the changed-FK case under the author's adapter behavior before\naltering the lazy-join lifecycle.\n"}
